The Dashboard only showed basic fleet status, tasks, and grouped alerts. This refactors it into a full macro view with 10 indicators across 4 card rows, sourced exclusively from Google Sheets (replacing the `api.js` dependency). Also removes the duplicate `cbmesp-header` that was being rendered both by the global `Header` component and inside `Dashboard.jsx` itself.

## `googleSheets.js` — new `getDashboardMacro()`
- Fetches `1SGB`, `2SGB`, `TAREFAS`, `MANUTENCOES`, `OS` in parallel via `Promise.allSettled` — missing sheets degrade gracefully to zero values
- Returns a single unified object covering all 10 indicators: fleet status, alerts count, pending tasks, maintenance spend/count, top-spending vehicle, oldest vehicle, vehicle types, and OS status

## `Dashboard.jsx` — complete replacement
- Imports only from `googleSheets.js`; `api.js` import removed
- Removes duplicate `.cbmesp-header` block (global `Header` in `App.jsx` already renders it)
- Four card rows:
  - **Status da Frota** — Operando / Baixadas / Reserva / Total (4 cards)
  - **Indicadores Macro** — Alertas / Tarefas Pendentes / Manutenções Realizadas / Gasto Total (4 cards, with red/orange variant styling when non-zero)
  - **Destaques** — Top Gasto / Viatura Mais Velha / Ordens de Serviço mini-table (3 cards)
  - **Tipos de Viatura** — colored chips extracted from prefixo (`ABS`, `TP`, `MO`, etc.)
- 5-minute auto-refresh + manual sync button + loading/error states preserved

## `Dashboard.css`
- Added `@media (max-width: 900px)` to collapse 4-col grids to 2-col and 3-col to 1-col

